  155\tautomatically.\n   156\t\n   157\t## Container Image Hardening\n   158\t\
n   159\tThe production `Dockerfile` ships the `yalla-api` binary and\n   160\t`
Dockerfile.worker` ships the `yalla-worker` binary inside a\n   161\t`gcr.io/dis
troless/static-debian12:nonroot` runtime so a leaked or\n   162\tcompromised ima
ge carries no shell, no package manager, no busybox,\n   163\tand no setuid bina
ries — only the service binary and the system CA\n   164\tbundle. The hardening 
posture is part of the public contract and is\n   165\tpinned by `internal/relea
se/container_hardening_static_test.go`; a\n   166\tregression in any one of the 
following is caught at build time:\n   167\t\n   168\t- **Multi-stage build.** T
he Go toolchain, module cache, and source\n   169\t  tree never reach the runtim
e layer. A single-stage Dockerfile is\n   170\t  rejected.\n   171\t- **Distrole
ss `nonroot` runtime.** The runtime stage\'s base image\n   172\t  is pinned to 
`gcr.io/distroless/static-debian12:nonroot` (UID/GID\n   173\t  65532). Debian/U
buntu/Alpine slim runtimes are rejected because\n   174\t  they reintroduce a sh
ell and a package manager.\n   175\t- **`USER nonroot:nonroot`.** The runtime st
age MUST run as the\n   176\t  non-root user. A missing or partial (`USER nonroo
t`) directive is\n   177\t  rejected.\n   178\t- **Hardened build flags.** The b
uilder stage MUST invoke\n   179\t  `go build` with `CGO_ENABLED=0` (static bina
ry compatible with\n   180\t  the distroless static image), `-trimpath` (strip l
ocal filesystem\n   181\t  paths from the binary), and `-ldflags="-s -w"` (drop 
the symbol\n   182\t  and DWARF tables). Each missing flag is a separate regress
ion.\n   183\t- **No `ADD <url>`.** Fetching arbitrary content at build time\n  
184\t  without checksum verification is forbidden. Use `COPY` or a\n   185\t  `R
UN curl ... | sha256sum -c` pattern.\n   186\t- **No baked secrets.** The Docker
file MUST NOT declare ENV values\n   187\t  whose key names contain `TOKEN`, `PA
SSWORD`, `SECRET`, `API_KEY`,\n   188\t  `PRIVATE_KEY`, `SIGNING_KEY`, or `DSN`.
Secrets are supplied by\n   189\t  the operator at runtime through environment v
ariables, never\n   190\t  baked into the image.\n   191\t- **No package install
in the runtime stage.** `apt-get`,\n   192\t  `apt install`, `yum install`, `dnf
install`, `microdnf install`,\n   193\t  and `apk add` are rejected in the final
layer. The builder stage\n   194\t  is free to install build dependencies; the r
untime stage is not.\n   195\t- **`COPY --from=builder --chown=nonroot:nonroot`.
** Every\n   196\t  cross-stage COPY into the runtime layer MUST chown to the\n 
 197\t  non-root user so the copied artefact is not owned by root.\n   198\t- **
Explicit `ENTRYPOINT`.** The runtime stage MUST declare an\n   199\t  `ENTRYPOIN
T` (not just `CMD`) so `docker run -- <args>` cannot\n   200\t  replace the bina
ry at launch.\n   201\t- **Worker image contract.** `Dockerfile.worker` MUST bui
ld\n   202\t  `./cmd/yalla-worker`, copy `/out/yalla-worker` to\n   203\t  `/usr
/local/bin/yalla-worker`, and use that binary as the\n   204\t  entrypoint. The 
worker has no HTTP listener, so orchestrators\n   205\t  should use process live
ness, non-zero exit restarts, durable\n   206\t  provisioning job state, dead-le
tter alerts, worker queue metrics,\n   207\t  and structured `service=yalla-work
er` logs instead of an in-image\n   208\t  HTTP health probe.\n   209\t\n   210\
tOperators are expected to run the image with `--read-only`,\n   211\t`--cap-dro
p=ALL`, and a non-host network. The Dockerfile\'s header\n   212\tcomment docume
